<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlos Salinas de Gortari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlos Salinas de Gortari was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> from 1988 to 1994 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/institutional-revolutionary-party">Institutional Revolutionary Party</a>, after an election widely accused of fraud. He privatised state companies, reformed the land-tenure provisions of the constitution and negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-american-free-trade-agreement">North American Free Trade Agreement</a>. His last year brought the Zapatista uprising and the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luis-donaldo-colosio">Luis Donaldo Colosio</a>, and the peso crisis followed weeks after he left office.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlos-salinas-de-gortari.jpg" alt="Carlos Salinas de Gortari" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrés Monroy · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlos_Salinas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
